1b:["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-12","children":[["$","section",null,{"id":"learn","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":1}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"Learn"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"How this works"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"Read this first. Everything after it assumes these ideas."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-8","children":[["$","section","0",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"What makes a sentence complete"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"A complete sentence needs three things: a subject, a main verb, and a thought that can stand on its own. Miss any one of them and you have a fragment — no matter how long the group of words is."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"That last point is where most people go wrong. Length feels like completeness. It is not. \"The manager, who had worked there for eleven years and knew every customer by name\" runs to sixteen words and is still a fragment, because the manager never does anything."}]],"$undefined","$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 max-w-[68ch] rounded-lg border-l-4 border-eng-gold-500 bg-eng-gold-50 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-gold-700","children":"The test"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":"Read the group of words aloud on its own. If a listener would wait for the rest, it is a fragment."}]]}]]}],["$","section","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"The two opposite errors"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"A fragment is too little — a piece of a sentence sent out alone. A run-on is too much — two complete sentences jammed together without the punctuation that separates them."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"A comma splice is the most common run-on and the hardest to see, because a comma looks like it is doing the job. It is not strong enough. Two complete sentences need a period, a semicolon, or a comma plus one of seven joining words."}]],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[36rem] border-collapse text-left text-sm","children":[["$","thead",null,{"className":"bg-eng-navy-50","children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","Join",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Join"}],["$","th","Use it when",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Use it when"}],["$","th","Example",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Example"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 align-top","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Period"}],"$L1e","$L1f"]}],"$L20","$L21","$L22"]}]]}]}],"$undefined"]}],"$L23"]}]]}],"$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27"]}]
