23:["$","section","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Agreement, and why it is really a subject problem"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"Subject-verb agreement errors are usually not verb errors. They are subject-identification errors. In \"The box of files ___ on the counter,\" the subject is box, not files — files sits inside a prepositional phrase, and a phrase never changes the subject."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-3 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":"Cross out every prepositional phrase before you choose the verb. The sentence gets shorter and the answer gets obvious."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mb-4 max-w-[68ch] space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Each, every, either, neither, and words ending in -one or -body are singular"}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Two subjects joined by and are plural"}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"With either/or and neither/nor, match the verb to the nearer subject"}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],[